  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "A jacket and a shirt originally sold for \\(\\$80\\) and \\(\\$40,\\) respectively. During a sale Chris bought the \\(\\$80\\) jacket at a \\(40\\%\\) discount and the \\(\\$40\\) shirt at a \\(55\\%\\) discount. The total amount saved was what percent of the total of the original prices?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(45\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(47\\tfrac12\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(50\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(79\\tfrac16\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(95\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Each discount applies to that item's original price, so first calculate the actual dollars saved. The jacket saves \\(80\\times0.40=32\\) dollars, and the shirt saves \\(40\\times0.55=22\\) dollars.\n\nThe total savings are therefore \\(32+22=54\\) dollars, compared with an original total price of \\(80+40=120\\) dollars. The percentage saved is\n\\[\n\\frac{54}{120}=0.45=45\\%.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(45\\%\\), choice A.",
